{
  "overview" : "Extend POST /shorten with optional customAlias and strictly-typed ttlSeconds, store an absolute UTC expiry on UrlMapping, and enforce alias uniqueness with a DB unique constraint on code. Translate DataIntegrityViolationException to 409 for aliases and regenerate for generated codes. Redirect returns 410 for expired links and keeps 404 for unknown codes. A thread-safe in-memory fixed-window per-IP rate limiter (RateLimitService) is invoked from a HandlerInterceptor on POST /shorten. The interceptor runs before body binding and validation, so every request counts and 429 takes precedence over 400/409. The interceptor uses request.getRemoteAddr() and ignores X-Forwarded-For. Limits come from application.yml (default 10 requests per 60s). An injectable Clock bean (util/ClockConfig) makes expiry and the rate window testable. ttlSeconds is bound as a JsonNode in ShortenRequest and parsed strictly in TtlValidator: only integral JSON numbers greater than 0 are accepted. This avoids Jackson coercion of 1.5 or \"5\". Aliases must match ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$ with length 3-32, are case-sensitive, and reserved route names are rejected. Existing rows keep a NULL expiry and are non-expiring. All new errors use the existing ErrorResponse(status, error, message) format. No config/ package is used, because it is not in the mandated layout.",
